    "methodology": "Both reviewer numbers are DECISION-WEIGHTED means over all 2,363,286 decisions in decision_view.parquet -- a population statistic, not a sample estimate. No seed/sampling procedure is involved because decision_view already IS the full population of decisions (candidate_count and optimal_candidate_count are exact per-decision counts). 'Optimal' means membership in the tied argmin set (regret==0), i.e. ties count as optimal. Regret is raw miss-count regret (y_loss - min_y_loss within the decision), unweighted by candidate count beyond the per-decision mean itself."
